    the name is not the symbol, but the lowercase name, e.g. one would use
    “`<Ctrl>minus`” instead of “`<Ctrl>-`”.

    Modifiers are enclosed in angular brackets `<>`, and match the
    Gdk.ModifierType mask:

    - `<Shift>` for `Gdk.ModifierType.SHIFT_MASK`
    - `<Ctrl>` for `Gdk.ModifierType.CONTROL_MASK`
    - `<Alt>` for `Gdk.ModifierType.ALT_MASK`
    - `<Meta>` for `Gdk.ModifierType.META_MASK`
    - `<Super>` for `Gdk.ModifierType.SUPER_MASK`
    - `<Hyper>` for `Gdk.ModifierType.HYPER_MASK`

    If the parse operation fails, accelerator_key and accelerator_mods will
    be set to 0 (zero).

    Args:
        accelerator: string representing an accelerator

    Returns:
        whether parsing succeeded
        accelerator_key: return location for accelerator keyval
        accelerator_mods: return location for accelerator
            modifier mask
    """

